  "implemented": [
    "Payer and operator income use shared canonical pool/index/membership checks with code/factory/custody, active value/math rules, canonical clock and revocable publication leases",
    "An existing encrypted operator credit can provide spend credentials below an imported history floor only through its original wallet and authenticated current note membership",
    "Current membership does not establish invoice timing or traffic entitlement; original receipt imports and channel-credit recovery retain historical verification",
    "Original historical membership material stays unchanged in financial records even when the current tree path differs after later appends",
    "Exclusive durable assignment of each operator note to one payer book survives pruning and process reopen",
    "Previously unassigned income can join the same book after pruning, once, without exporting keys or moving funds through public balances",
    "Mixed original payer and operator keys can consolidate notes after checkpoint import; an exact earned-note withdrawal needs no output/change note",
    "Each unspent income provider must be unlocked and reattached after reopen; spent income does not require credentials for unrelated directly owned funds"
  ],
